 MID360/IMU mounting, corrected Livox topics, joystick buttons, command-source
 toggle, namespace, and safe-start guard are shared with the legacy entry point.
 
+Terrain navigation consumes `/cmd_vel` at **unity gain** for linear X/Y and
+angular Z. Commands are already in m/s and rad/s: `(0.4, 0.2, 0.3)` is passed to
+the terrain policy as `(0.4, 0.2, 0.3)`. The input limits are ±0.7 m/s for X,
+±0.5 m/s for Y and ±1.0 rad/s for yaw. Both Nav2 and custom Pure Pursuit use this path. The
+previous adapter amplified X by 2 and Y/yaw by 1.5 within those input limits.
+Joystick axis conversion and the trained actor's observation normalization
+are separate and unchanged. Policy response still needs closed-loop validation;
+unity command gain does not guarantee exact physical velocity tracking.
+
+After rebuilding `rubi_gazebo_plugins`, restart Gazebo to load the new library.
+When simulation time resets, restart localization and navigation as well, then
+relocalize and send a new goal. Saved map files are not affected.
+
